WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.452
Because a materialized view stores rows, Postgres can index those rows.

00:00:06.096 --> 00:00:09.808
This example creates a unique index on diagnosis.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:17.428
Indexes may support faster reads and are also relevant to certain Postgres concurrent refresh requirements.

00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:24.742
Choose indexes based on real query patterns and constraints, not simply because the object is materialized.
